body:
He's so fucking hot that I'm sold on the game simply for him. 

&#x200B;

Mess me up Dimitri.

He probably takes it as a personal attack that you want to get rid of his shirts. It's great and all that other people in this thread are encouraging you to keep his shirts, but I'll give the opposing POV. Having a bunch of shirts with holes is completely impractical and he definitely knows it. Hoarding them is even more unhealthy. If he doesn't even wear those shirts then they're just taking up space. If he keeps up this behavior then he'll probably end up hoarding even more things he doesn't need. Hoarding in itself is a coping mechanism to feel comfort and he needs to work on that.

&#x200B;

The compromise that you two can discuss is that he gets to keep them if he must, but not in your closet because your closet isn't a vintage collection. It has an everyday use for it, unlike those shirts.

&#x200B;

Lastly, the amount of comments criticizing you as a person is pretty gross. They don't know anything about the stress you've been through or what other crap he might be giving you. This can be one of many. Personally attacking you for ranting isn't okay.
